<p class="lead"><strong>Thank you to everyone who completed the recent survey, shared evidence or volunteered.</strong> The results show a range of views. The clearest priority was to prepare for a possible legal route, while continuing to build evidence, give owners a public voice and test whether JLR's individual-case approach produces lasting outcomes.</p>

<p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/updates/october-2026-member-priorities/">See the published October survey results</a></p>

<h2>Legal preparation and coordination</h2>

We are coordinating legal preparation in the UK, with local leads joining as other regions come on line. Tim is helping lead this work alongside new volunteers. It is preparation, not a claim: any representation, proceedings or costs would need separate, explicit authority from eligible members.

If you may want to take part in a future UK process, please make sure your <a href="/member/account/">legal name and formal contact address are recorded privately in My Data</a>. That helps avoid delay if members later choose to take a defined next step.

<h2>More member stories, wider reach</h2>

We have built a member-stories feature so owners can prepare an account of their experience with photos or video. With separate publication permission, a story can help our website, social channels and press packs. It is in final testing: <a href="/member/account/">register interest in trying new member features</a> if you would like to help test it before wider release.

Our reach is growing on several fronts. Ole is leading our Northern Europe efforts from Norway, and Kevin is leading Southern Europe from France. Kevin also brings the respect he has earned through his longstanding presence on <a href="https://www.ipaceforums.co.uk/f">I-PACE Forums</a>. Thank you both, and everyone giving time, evidence or introductions.

<h2>Evidence: document imports next</h2>

We are working on a secure in-browser way to import service information and documents into your private record. It is still in development, but the aim is simple: make it easier to retain the facts that matter without emailing sensitive documents around.

<h2>The unanswered battery question</h2>

JLR says cases will be considered individually, including warranty or goodwill factors. The unanswered question is simpler: if a module fails outside the high-voltage warranty, is it treated as a safety concern or as chargeable degradation? With diagnosis and replacement potentially costing hundreds or thousands of pounds, that distinction matters. H572 is still unannounced, so its scope and what it means for future module failures remain unknown.

